{
  "name": "ultrathink-coder",
  "parameters": [
    {"name": "TASK", "type_name": "str", "description": "The coding task / feature to implement"}
  ],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "name": "cache_check",
      "op": "QMEM",
      "attributes": {
        "query": "{{TASK}}",
        "memory_tier": "ltm"
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 2,
      "name": "think_architect",
      "op": "THINK",
      "attributes": {
        "template_str": "ultrathink. You are a Rust systems architect reviewing the APXM project at ~/projects/agents/apxm.\n\nRead the relevant source files first. Then produce a detailed architectural plan:\n- Which crates are affected and why\n- Exact file paths to create or modify\n- Public API design (structs, traits, function signatures)\n- How it integrates with existing systems (ContextStack, MemoCache, Scheduler)\n- Potential architectural risks\n\nTask: {{TASK}}",
        "budget": 8000
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 3,
      "name": "think_adversary",
      "op": "REASON",
      "attributes": {
        "template_str": "ultrathink. You are a senior engineer whose job is to find flaws BEFORE code is written.\n\nAnalyze this task and identify:\n- Hidden complexity the architect will miss\n- API decisions that will cause regret in 6 months\n- Race conditions or unsafety in concurrent code\n- Missing error cases and edge cases\n- What NOT to build (scope creep traps)\n- The minimal correct solution vs the over-engineered one\n\nTask: {{TASK}}\n\nProject: ~/projects/agents/apxm (Rust, tokio async, rayon parallel scheduler)"
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 4,
      "name": "think_impl_expert",
      "op": "THINK",
      "attributes": {
        "template_str": "ultrathink. You are a Rust implementation expert focused on correctness and testability.\n\nFor this task, produce:\n- Complete Rust code blocks (not pseudocode) for the key structs and impls\n- Unit test cases covering happy path + error paths + edge cases\n- Integration test approach\n- Exact cargo.toml dependency additions needed\n- Build command: `dekk apxm build` (not bare cargo build)\n\nTask: {{TASK}}\n\nProject: ~/projects/agents/apxm",
        "budget": 8000
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 5,
      "name": "sync_planners",
      "op": "WAIT_ALL",
      "attributes": {
        "tokens": ["{{node_2}}", "{{node_3}}", "{{node_4}}"]
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 6,
      "name": "merge_plans",
      "op": "MERGE",
      "attributes": {
        "strategy": "concat",
        "tokens": ["{{node_2}}", "{{node_3}}", "{{node_4}}"]
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 7,
      "name": "synthesize",
      "op": "THINK",
      "attributes": {
        "template_str": "ultrathink. You have 3 expert analyses of the same coding task:\n1. Architect plan (what to build + API design)\n2. Adversary review (what will go wrong + what NOT to build)\n3. Implementation expert (exact code + tests)\n\nSynthesize into ONE unified implementation brief:\n- Resolve all conflicts (when architect and adversary disagree, adversary wins on scope)\n- Include exact file paths and complete Rust code blocks\n- Include test cases\n- Flag remaining uncertainty with [RISK: ...]\n- End with a CONSERVATIVE APPROACH section and a BOLD APPROACH section\n\nAll three analyses:\n{0}",
        "budget": 12000
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 8,
      "name": "format_conservative_prompt",
      "op": "THINK",
      "attributes": {
        "template_str": "Extract the CONSERVATIVE APPROACH from this synthesis and format it as a precise instruction for a coding agent.\n\nRequirements:\n- Start with: cd ~/projects/agents/apxm\n- List exact files to create/edit with full content\n- End with: Run 'dekk apxm build'. Fix all errors. Run 'cargo test -p <affected_crate>'. Run 'git add -A && git commit -m feat: <description> (conservative)'\n- Be extremely precise — the agent executes this literally\n\nSynthesis:\n{0}",
        "budget": 3000
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 9,
      "name": "format_bold_prompt",
      "op": "THINK",
      "attributes": {
        "template_str": "Extract the BOLD APPROACH from this synthesis and format it as a precise instruction for a coding agent.\n\nRequirements:\n- Start with: cd ~/projects/agents/apxm\n- List exact files to create/edit with full content\n- End with: Run 'dekk apxm build'. Fix all errors. Run 'cargo test -p <affected_crate>'. Run 'git add -A && git commit -m feat: <description> (bold)'\n- Be extremely precise — the agent executes this literally\n\nSynthesis:\n{0}",
        "budget": 3000
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 10,
      "name": "sync_prompts",
      "op": "WAIT_ALL",
      "attributes": {
        "tokens": ["{{node_8}}", "{{node_9}}"]
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 11,
      "name": "spawn_conservative",
      "op": "SPAWN_AGENT",
      "attributes": {
        "agent_name": "conservative_coder",
        "profile": "codex",
        "cwd": "$APXM_HOME"
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 12,
      "name": "spawn_bold",
      "op": "SPAWN_AGENT",
      "attributes": {
        "agent_name": "bold_coder",
        "profile": "claude",
        "cwd": "$APXM_HOME"
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 13,
      "name": "run_conservative",
      "op": "COMMUNICATE",
      "attributes": {
        "recipient": "conservative_coder",
        "protocol": "acp"
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 14,
      "name": "run_bold",
      "op": "COMMUNICATE",
      "attributes": {
        "recipient": "bold_coder",
        "protocol": "acp"
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 15,
      "name": "sync_implementations",
      "op": "WAIT_ALL",
      "attributes": {
        "tokens": ["{{node_13}}", "{{node_14}}"]
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 16,
      "name": "verify",
      "op": "VERIFY",
      "attributes": {
        "claim": "Both implementations build and all tests pass",
        "evidence": "{{node_13}} {{node_14}}"
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 17,
      "name": "reflect_and_pick",
      "op": "REFLECT",
      "attributes": {
        "trace_query": "last_execution",
        "reflection_prompt": "Two implementations were attempted in parallel (conservative + bold). Review both outcomes and the verification result. Pick one winner.\n\nConservative result: {{node_13}}\nBold result: {{node_14}}\nVerification: {{node_16}}\n\nOutput: WINNER: [conservative|bold] and a one-paragraph explanation."
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 18,
      "name": "store_solution",
      "op": "UMEM",
      "attributes": {
        "key": "{{TASK}}",
        "value": "{{node_17}}",
        "memory_tier": "ltm"
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 19,
      "name": "final_report",
      "op": "PRINT",
      "attributes": {
        "message": "=== ULTRATHINK COMPLETE ===\n{{node_17}}"
      }
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
    {"from": 1, "to": 2, "dependency": "Control"},
    {"from": 1, "to": 3, "dependency": "Control"},
    {"from": 1, "to": 4, "dependency": "Control"},

    {"from": 2, "to": 5, "dependency": "Data"},
    {"from": 3, "to": 5, "dependency": "Data"},
    {"from": 4, "to": 5, "dependency": "Data"},

    {"from": 2, "to": 6, "dependency": "Data"},
    {"from": 3, "to": 6, "dependency": "Data"},
    {"from": 4, "to": 6, "dependency": "Data"},
    {"from": 5, "to": 6, "dependency": "Control"},

    {"from": 6, "to": 7, "dependency": "Data"},

    {"from": 7, "to": 8, "dependency": "Data"},
    {"from": 7, "to": 9, "dependency": "Data"},

    {"from": 8, "to": 10, "dependency": "Data"},
    {"from": 9, "to": 10, "dependency": "Data"},

    {"from": 10, "to": 11, "dependency": "Control"},
    {"from": 10, "to": 12, "dependency": "Control"},

    {"from": 11, "to": 13, "dependency": "Data"},
    {"from": 8, "to": 13, "dependency": "Data"},

    {"from": 12, "to": 14, "dependency": "Data"},
    {"from": 9, "to": 14, "dependency": "Data"},

    {"from": 13, "to": 15, "dependency": "Data"},
    {"from": 14, "to": 15, "dependency": "Data"},

    {"from": 15, "to": 16, "dependency": "Data"},

    {"from": 16, "to": 17, "dependency": "Data"},
    {"from": 13, "to": 17, "dependency": "Data"},
    {"from": 14, "to": 17, "dependency": "Data"},

    {"from": 17, "to": 18, "dependency": "Data"},
    {"from": 18, "to": 19, "dependency": "Data"}
  ],
  "metadata": {
    "description": "Ultrathink coding workflow: parallel speculative planning + adversarial review + dual implementation race + verification + LTM cache. Structurally outperforms single Claude Code or Codex on complex tasks.",
    "pattern": "QMEM(ltm) → 3x parallel THINK+REASON+THINK → WAIT_ALL → MERGE → THINK(ultrathink synth) → 2x parallel SPAWN+COMMUNICATE → WAIT_ALL → VERIFY → REFLECT(pick winner) → UMEM(ltm) → PRINT",
    "performance_advantages": [
      "LTM cache hit: instant return on repeat or similar tasks",
      "Parallel planning: architect + adversary + impl-expert run simultaneously",
      "Adversarial pre-flight: REASON catches mistakes before any code is written",
      "Dual speculative implementation: conservative (codex) vs bold (claude) race in parallel",
      "Hard VERIFY gate: build + tests must pass",
      "REFLECT picks winner based on actual evidence",
      "UMEM stores solution for future cache hits"
    ],
    "ops_used": ["QMEM", "THINK", "REASON", "WAIT_ALL", "MERGE", "SPAWN_AGENT", "COMMUNICATE", "VERIFY", "REFLECT", "UMEM", "PRINT"],
    "vs_single_agent": "Same wall time on planning (parallel), 2x speculative coverage on implementation, adversarial review eliminates 'confident but wrong' failures"
  }
}
